to people who think locals like  humanitarian aid workers i would say  that this is not necessarily  true i wouldn't approach it in the sense  that  they will be automatically grateful that  you're here  they didn't really ask you to to come so  the best thing is to be humble  and let's not forget that the local  populations are often also aware of  the contradictory relationships that can  be  present especially from western  countries where they might be  involved in the conflict by selling arms  etc or supporting a certain side  so basically i would recommend actually  approaching local people with an open  ear and really try to listen to what are  their needs what they need  and to try to build a relationship with  the direct beneficiaries not necessarily  you know authorities or representatives  but really the people on the ground who  are really in the need  um i think it is important to build a  relationship with them  and to listen to them and at the end  this is actually the  fulfilling part or where you can  actually gain acceptance
 

